+# Agent Note: Complete archived session deletion
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-05-complete-session-deletion.zh.md)
+## Problem
+
+The delete RPC removed durable records while retaining idle Agent and Session objects. Subsequent writes could recreate the log. Persistence deletion also flushed write-behind while holding the same serialization queue used by the flush, creating a deadlock.
+
+## Decision
+
+The API gateway retains the AgentHandle it receives when creating or resuming sessions. Deletion refuses running, transitioning, or externally owned sessions. It disposes its owned idle handle, then asks persistence to delete, then removes workspace and archive indexes. Creation is rejected while deletion is in progress.
+
+Persistence rejects live sessions and awaits retirement before entering its per-id deletion queue. Backend failure preserves tracked state for retry. The archive UI retains IDs whose metadata disappeared, so partial failures remain actionable.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Deleting only the on-disk artifact leaves active writers. Disposing arbitrary registered agents violates ownership. Flushing inside the deletion queue cannot complete because flush appends through that queue.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Hosts must restart to acquire the new ownership bookkeeping. Running sessions must finish or stop before deletion. The gateway only disposes agents it owns. Focused tests cover storage failure retry and foreign ownership; JSONL and SQLite contract tests reopen storage after deletion. A keyless real Web composition snapshot asserts absence from all five runtime and persistence views.
